{
  "appliesWhen": "([.metadata.component // empty] + [.components[]?]) | map(select(.type==\"machine-learning-model\")) | length > 0",
  "subject": "([.metadata.component // empty] + [.components[]?]) | map(select(.type==\"machine-learning-model\"))",
  "subjectLabel": "model component",
  "emptySubjectDetail": "no machine-learning-model components",
  "spec": "G7 Software Bill of Materials for AI — Minimum Elements (BSI/ACN et al., 2026-05)",
  "note": "Declarative map of the 50 G7 minimum elements (7 clusters) to CycloneDX 1.7 ML-BOM checks. Read by validate-sbom.sh's registry evaluator, which binds $subjects = the components the registry declares as its subject (here machine-learning-model components) once per run. Element shapes: 'cdxPath' is a jq boolean over the whole SBOM (pass / not present); 'missingPath' is a jq expression (may use $subjects) returning the names of model components MISSING the element — per-model coverage, so one unlicensed model in a multi-model SBOM warns with the offender listed instead of passing on any-model presence; when both are null the element has no automated source and is surfaced as 'requires human review'. 'source' records where a satisfied value comes from: auto (read directly), inferred (derived from signals), declared (present only if a human/manifest supplied it), na (no automated source). 'role' is informational — the party the G7 text names as the provider — NOT a required/optional gate (the G7 document defines no per-role required matrix). Openness (open weight/architecture/data/training) is not a separate G7 element; the spec lists it as an example facet of 'Model license', so g7-model-openness is grouped under models and tied to the license element; it accepts either openness:* properties (written by enrich-aibom.sh) or a prose declaration anywhere in the SBOM, so supplier SBOMs that state openness in text still count.",
  "clusters": [
    {
      "id": "metadata",
      "title": "Metadata",
      "name": "Metadata",
      "name_ko": "메타데이터",
      "name_zh": "後設資料",
      "elements": [
        {
